.TH "SKARN-EULA" "1" "2026-06-23" "skarn 0.18.0" "Skarn Manual"
.SH NAME
skarn\-eula \- Print the Skarn End User License Agreement, or record
acceptance of the current version (accept)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskarn\fR \fBeula\fR [accept]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the End User License Agreement embedded in the binary (the same text
distributed as EULA.md and published at https://getskarn.com/terms/), or
record acceptance of the current agreement version with `skarn eula accept`.
Skarn presents the agreement on first run: on a terminal it asks for
acceptance before the invoked command runs (declining exits 1 and performs no
operation; the next run asks again), and in a non\-interactive run (CI, pipes,
containers) it prints a one\-line notice on stderr and proceeds \- running
Skarn constitutes acceptance, and recording it with `skarn eula accept`
silences the notice. Acceptance is recorded locally in
~/.config/skarn/eula\-accepted.json (honoring $XDG_CONFIG_HOME) and never
transmitted; installing a License Token with `skarn license <file>` records it
too, mirroring the acceptance given on the registration form. A record that
cannot be written never blocks the run \- Skarn proceeds and asks again next
time. Reading the agreement never requires accepting it first: `skarn eula`,
`\-\-help`, `\-\-version`, bare `skarn`, `skarn completion`, `skarn doctor`,
and every form of `skarn guard` run without the acceptance interaction. When a
new agreement version is published, a changed major version re\-prompts; a
minor change prints a one\-line notice and continues. SKARN_EULA_ACCEPTED=1
suppresses the interaction for a run without recording anything.
.PP
The agreement surface takes no flags: `skarn eula` prints the embedded
agreement text, `skarn eula accept` records acceptance of the current version.
Both work before acceptance.
